1
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(New bonus scenes)

2
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:08,100
(Too immersed in the mystery
to even look for a pen)

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:09,790
Ning is unusually cheerful today.

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,180
(Already sees through it)
He must have a role.

5
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:12,020
(Ke watching the show)

6
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,030
What is it?

7
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:13,910
(Deduction mode activated)
What we just said was,

8
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:14,910
right now,

9
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:15,910
one of us

10
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:16,990
is our 2030 self.

11
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,910
What if our 2030 self came back

12
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:20,710
(Ning-style deduction)
and was killed by our 2016 self?

13
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:21,910
I was going to kill them first.

14
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:23,710
(Stops to analyze)
If it's someone from 2016,

15
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:24,390
they could just say

16
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,350
it was self-defense.

17
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,350
(Self-defense)
Right, self-defense.

18
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:28,390
But for some reason, they don't know

19
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:29,910
who this is.

20
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:30,790
(Imagination runs wild)
And why do he look exactly like me?

21
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:31,390
I'll stab you to death.

22
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:31,990
I'll burn you.

23
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,430
Now that this is happening,

24
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:34,310
just say it.

25
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:34,790
Who is it?

26
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:35,350
If I say it,

27
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,630
I won't be legally responsible, right?

28
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:37,550
(Gets tricked into talking)
It's you, isn't it?

29
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:38,100
No.

30
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:38,820
(Trap successful)

31
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:40,110
Here's the logic.

32
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:41,590
(Serious explanation)
The killer still has to hide, right?

33
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,310
And when you see someone

34
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:44,030
who looks exactly like you,

35
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:44,910
your first instinct is to kill them.

36
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:45,830
Does that make sense?

37
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:46,470
No,

38
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:47,420
you come over and kill me.

39
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:48,060
(Passionate acting)

40
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:48,790
Ning.

41
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,550
(No one else fits)
It can only be you.

42
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,460
So it's just me and Ke.

43
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:53,790
(Ning is pretty cute)
So it's just me and Ke.

44
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:55,860
(What did I do?)

45
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:56,580
(Just one blank sheet)

46
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,190
(Forgot the pen while deducing)
Where's the pen? Give me one.

47
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:59,260
There's no red pen.

48
00:00:59,260 --> 00:00:59,700
(Searching for a pen mode)

49
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:00,620
(Looking left)

50
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:01,900
(Looking right)

51
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:06,380
(Busy searching everywhere)

52
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,190
(Carefully searching)
Looking for the pen.

53
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,100
(I think it's here)

54
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:11,620
It's here!

55
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:12,180
(Found it!)

56
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:13,550
I knew I could count on you.

57
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:15,030
(As expected of Ding)
I knew I could count on Ding.

58
00:01:15,860 --> 00:01:16,860
(Done)

59
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:19,860
(If there were a time machine,
the deduction team would want one)

60
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:21,670
(About to travel through time)
This is a time machine.

61
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:24,390
Maybe.

62
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:26,870
(Ke, now free across time and space)
We can go wherever we want.

63
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,430
(Dreaming of the future)
I want to go to 2036.

64
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:29,990
(I'm going way ahead)
I want to go to 3030.

65
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,790
Can we?

66
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:32,230
(Let's go to the future together)
Let's go to the future together.

67
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:33,510
(I agree)
I think so too.

68
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:34,510
What else are we playing?

69
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:36,220
(You're something else)

70
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:37,510
(That's enough!)
Let's go back.

71
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:38,670
Let's go, everyone.

72
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:41,710
(Can't believe it)
Can we really?

73
00:01:41,710 --> 00:01:42,300
Really.

74
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:42,790
I'll write...

75
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:43,710
Where do you want to go?

76
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:45,240
(Wants to go to 2027)
2027.

77
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,110
2027?

78
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,010
(Oh?)
Why?

79
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:49,910
You know what 2026 will be like?

80
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,150
In 2026, you joined a variety show

81
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:53,950
(I'm a prophet)
called The Truth Season 4.

82
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:55,580
(There he goes again, Dad)

83
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:58,110
Do you want to go back
to the past or into the future?

84
00:01:58,360 --> 00:01:59,550
(I want the future)
Go to the future.

85
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:01,510
(Back to the past)
I think I'd go back to the past.

86
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:02,390
Why?

87
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,190
(Back to the past +1)
Me too.

88
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,950
(Online application to turn back time)
There are times I'd like to go back.

89
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:06,470
(I want to know too)
Why go back?

90
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:08,310
What year would you go back to?

91
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:10,390
(Returning to school days)
I'd go back to when I was in school.

92
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,260
(I feel you)
Yeah, me too.

93
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:13,830
(Missing school days)
I kind of miss it.

94
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,550
You can go back to school now.

95
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,390
(One side: the sentimental F-type)
Go back to middle or high school.

96
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:18,830
Sure.

97
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:21,190
(Other side: the practical T-type)
Do you remember any lottery numbers?

98
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:23,470
If you went back,
could you use a cheat code?

99
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:26,030
Yeah. Then I'd go back to 2000.

100
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,990
Buy more WeTV shares.

101
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:30,340
(So visionary)

102
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:34,140
(Who's the pun king
of the deduction team?)

103
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:35,740
(Guess the idiom from the picture)
Who are you?

104
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:36,710
Who?

105
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:37,750
Who are you?

106
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,910
They're respectively...

107
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:40,290
Radish and greens.

108
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:41,060
Each has its own appeal.

109
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:41,590
Bitter melon.

110
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:42,550
And bitter melon.

111
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:44,470
(Veggies don't know each other)
Veggies don't know each other

112
00:02:44,470 --> 00:02:45,750
Who won in the end?

113
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,150
Wait, what's this fruit?

114
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:48,830
Let me see.

115
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:52,780
Vegetables, bitter melon, carrots.

116
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:53,380
(Reading the clues)

117
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:54,750
Meet someone...

118
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:56,060
meet someone unfamiliar.

119
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:57,190
Unfamiliar with what?

120
00:02:57,750 --> 00:02:58,470
Meet someone unlucky.

121
00:02:58,480 --> 00:02:59,440
You mean meet someone unlucky?

122
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:00,380
Meet someone unlucky.

123
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:01,870
Right and wrong?

124
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:02,980
(Right and wrong)
Meet someone unfamiliar.

125
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:03,750
Why?

126
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:04,510
Because you met someone

127
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,230
you weren't familiar with.

128
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,950
Who are you?

129
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:09,710
What kind of phrase is meet
someone unfamiliar?

130
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:11,750
It's meet someone unlucky.

131
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:12,310
Right.

132
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:13,340
There's no Y.

133
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:13,950
No Y.

134
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,430
Then it's vegetable.

135
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:16,830
Which vegetable?

136
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,550
(Dead serious)
Cai Cai, who am I?

137
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:19,670
(Cai Cai, who am I?)
Guess who I am.

138
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:21,990
Three Cai,
and there are three of them.

139
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,150
Three Cai.

140
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:25,060
(Ning's already ordering food)
Three dishes and a soup.

141
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:26,550
Cousin, Uncle.

142
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:27,860
Uncle, Zhang Fei.

143
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:28,820
(Cousin? Uncle? Zhang Fei?)

144
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:30,310
(Soul-searching question)
Can we use actual idioms?

145
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:32,110
She's just playing with words.

146
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,230
She's literally just saying words.

147
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,070
Look, here.

148
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:36,750
The 2nd Pun King Challenge!

149
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:38,030
(Ning, judge mode)
Four contestants.

150
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:39,710
Three, two, one, go!

151
00:03:39,710 --> 00:03:40,960
Round 1.

152
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:42,080
Right and wrong.

153
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:43,430
Nonsense.

154
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,910
Three kingdoms divided.

155
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:47,430
I was still thinking Peach Garden Oath.

156
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,990
Sheng, Ku, Hu.

157
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,230
Carrot, lettuce, bitter melon.

158
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:53,790
Does it have something
to do with the vegetables?

159
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:54,390
Probably not.

160
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:57,110
(Pun King's intuition)
Three veggies don't fit an idiom.

161
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,630
It must have something
to do with them being vegetables.

162
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:00,750
(Almost there!)
The vegetables don't know each other.

163
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:03,070
Right, they're strangers.

164
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:05,680
The vegetables don't know each other.

165
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,210
The plain vegetables
don't know each other.

166
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,950
Strangers to each other.

167
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:11,190
Strangers to each other.

168
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:12,110
Maybe.

169
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:14,230
(Excited)
Did I win?

170
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,950
Strangers to each other.

171
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:17,870
Vegetables.

172
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:19,630
Looks like your master taught you well.

173
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:20,670
Puns.

174
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,790
(Successfully opened)
That's a bit much.

175
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:27,100
(One more)

176
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:28,020
(Another one)

177
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:28,700
(Face it with a smile)

178
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:30,710
(Guess the idiom)
Is it a bird?

179
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:32,510
Bird doctor in charge.

180
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:34,310
Birds singing, flowers blooming.

181
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:37,030
Birds singing kind of sounds like bird.

182
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:38,430
Three handsome guys,

183
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:40,670
you three need both beauty

184
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,550
(Who will be the Pun King?)
and brains.

185
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:43,710
This is my black hole.

186
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:46,950
This bird is blindly playing doctor.

187
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:48,310
And this guy is just agreeing.

188
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:49,390
(Jin doesn't get it)
Blindly agreeing.

189
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,300
See a bird doctor.

190
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:52,420
(Ning being funny)

191
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:53,340
See a bird doctor.

192
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,550
Does the bird care about you?

193
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:56,600
I'll see if the bird cares about you.

194
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:57,780
(Not missing a single pun)

195
00:04:58,440 --> 00:04:58,830
Bird...

196
00:04:58,840 --> 00:04:59,950
Thanks, though.

197
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:01,030
So polite.

198
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:03,310
(Determined look)
Medical bird accident.

199
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:06,510
Medical...
you're really forcing the pun.

200
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:07,540
(Jin finds it cute)
But it's pretty cute.

201
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:08,260
Pretty cute.

202
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:09,950
Medical bird accident.

203
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:13,750
Could this be the hardest one?

204
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:14,910
Probably not.

205
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,990
The bird is right.

206
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:17,230
Bird is right.

207
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:19,310
(To a bird? Play music?)
Play music to a bird.

208
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:20,220
Play music to a bird.

209
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:21,350
(My silly son)
Where's the music?

210
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:25,070
(Wen is getting serious)
If a bird is seeing a doctor,

211
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,670
the bird doctor, doctor...

212
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:30,640
Bird.

213
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:34,700
A bird nestling against someone!

214
00:05:34,890 --> 00:05:36,520
A bird nestling against someone!

215
00:05:39,180 --> 00:05:40,540
(Gotta hand it to you)

216
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:42,380
(It takes a Pun King)

217
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:44,070
This must be it!

218
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:46,470
(Still the Pun King)
You're still...

219
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:47,950
Defending the title.

220
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:50,090
A bird nestling against someone.

221
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:52,430
A bird nestling against someone, right?

222
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:53,310
Definitely.

223
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:54,470
(One new fan gained)
This one's definitely right.

224
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,390
That's awesome.

225
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:58,540
(The Starting Line-Up's
go-to action guy)

226
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:00,150
Why didn't anyone
twist it open and smell it?

227
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,190
What was that?

228
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:02,950
Didn't you open it?

229
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:03,980
(Did I lose my memory?)

230
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,070
No, we didn't.

231
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:05,960
You didn't?

232
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:07,060
(Dizzy)

233
00:06:07,060 --> 00:06:08,140
(The truth is...)

234
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:08,950
Is this oil?

235
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:11,100
(Unscrews the cap)

236
00:06:14,940 --> 00:06:16,180
(It technically wasn't opened)

237
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:17,100
No one opened it.

238
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:17,820
(Insisting)

239
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:18,710
The cap was still on.

240
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,430
It was still sealed.

241
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:22,780
Let's send someone through again.

242
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:23,260
(Making a backup plan)

243
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:24,150
(Agreed +1)
Sure.

244
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,310
(Agreed +2)
Let's go.

245
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:26,350
Back to work.

246
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:27,860
(The doer takes action)
Okay, let's go.

247
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:28,710
Go through.

248
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,020
(Expectant look)
Are we going through?

249
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:31,340
(Determined)

250
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,270
Go back through.

251
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:34,020
(The team grows)

252
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:35,230
We're really going through?

253
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:35,950
(No hesitation)
Let's go back through.

254
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:37,700
We're here to catch the killer today.

255
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:39,340
(Clear goal)

256
00:06:39,380 --> 00:06:41,420
(Immersed in a discussion about parenting)

257
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,180
(Family education
debate in full swing)

258
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:45,190
How can you be like this?

259
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:47,870
(Seriously?)
Did you even spend time with them?

260
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:51,310
What right do you have to judge others?

261
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:52,870
I'm trying to...

262
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:55,030
Still blaming me to this day.

263
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,750
No, this is how we...

264
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:59,750
(Discipline officer mode!)
Talk all you want, but put that down.

265
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:01,420
(Play first, talk later)

266
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:02,870
Let me start with my parenting style.

267
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:04,590
I think when we were kids,

268
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:06,270
(From our experience)
our parents were pretty strict with us.

269
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,190
So I think children should choose

270
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,710
what they want to do themselves.

271
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:10,550
(Fully agrees)
Right?

272
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:12,470
So I don't think there's anything
wrong with my approach.

273
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:14,670
(What do you think?)
But the absent father is a problem.

274
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:15,510
When the kids talked,

275
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:16,790
(Father has zero presence)
they didn't even mention their father.

276
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:18,870
I get it now.

277
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:21,510
You four are completely warped.

278
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:23,350
(Immersed in character)
Totally absorbed in your roles.

279
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:26,230
After being treated so badly by An Yi,

280
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:29,270
your personalities have developed flaws

281
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:31,270
And gone to extremes.

282
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:32,350
We can't say

283
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:33,630
these parents

284
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:35,630
are completely in the wrong,

285
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:39,150
especially parents like Ning and Wen.

286
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:40,310
But I think

287
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:42,990
(Family observer)
parenting needs balance.

288
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,110
(Agreed +1)
Right.

289
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:46,390
What I want to say is,
we're all first-time humans.

290
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,750
(Ning is too immersed)
Why should I give in to him?

291
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:50,350
Well said.

292
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:51,830
Who isn't someone's son?

293
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:53,550
(Too into the role)
Wait, that's his point!

294
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:54,870
If I'm wrong, I'll admit it.

295
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:56,150
(Self-reflecting)
I'll be a good parent.

296
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:56,670
See?

297
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,950
She turned it around.

298
00:07:58,480 --> 00:07:59,070
Where did it go wrong?

299
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:00,710
My son

300
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:01,830
is an Aquarius.

301
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,350
(Based on his zodiac sign)
He's sensitive and cries easily.

302
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:03,990
Right?

303
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,830
I'm a Gemini, so maybe

304
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:06,750
our signs just don't get along.

305
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,870
Let's not talk about zodiac signs.

306
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:09,470
What about anything
besides zodiac signs?

307
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:11,390
I admit I haven't given
my child enough attention.

308
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:13,110
I gave him too much freedom.

309
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:15,550
(Self-reflecting mom)
I'll work on that from now on.

310
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:20,230
=The Truth (Season 4)=

311
00:08:20,230 --> 00:08:21,530
(SVIP updates Wed & Thu at 12PM.)

312
00:08:21,530 --> 00:08:22,380
(VIP updates next day at 12PM,
one week early.)
